  "id": "COMPOUND:32274 - PROTEIN:2641",
  "verbalization": "Dysienone appears to interact with the EDD domain protein, DegV family through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Dysienone directly targets CWR22R, which in turn is a target of Pubescenone and another compound, (3R,4aR,8aR)-8a-methyl-5-methylidene-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-1,2,3,4,4a,6,7,8-octahydronaphthalene. This latter compound also targets the EDD domain protein, DegV family. Additionally, Dysienone is linked to Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is a target of L-carvenyl acetate, which also targets the EDD domain protein, DegV family. These findings collectively indicate that Dysienone may influence the EDD domain protein, DegV family through a series of intermediates, possibly via metabolic or signaling pathways. The integration of these targets suggests a potential role for Dysienone in modulating the activity of the EDD domain protein, DegV family, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
